---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Approach" description="A practical Assess, Build, Handoff approach focused on maintainability, ownership, accessibility, security, and clear documentation.">
<section class="page-hero"><div class="container readable"><p class="eyebrow">Approach</p><h1>Start with the need. Keep the solution understandable.</h1><p class="lede">Good technical work should leave a business with clearer ownership and fewer avoidable surprises, not a system that only one person can operate.</p></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="flow"><article class="flow__step"><h2>Assess</h2><p>Inventory the current state, clarify the outcome, identify constraints, and understand ownership, cost, privacy, security, and maintenance requirements.</p></article><article class="flow__step"><h2>Build</h2><p>Choose a proportionate architecture, work through version-controlled changes, test what matters, and avoid recurring services that exist only for convenience.</p></article><article class="flow__step"><h2>Handoff</h2><p>Document deployment, access, recovery, rollback, and maintenance. Put business assets in the appropriate owner accounts and use named access for administration.</p></article></div></div></section>
<section class="section section--navy"><div class="container principle"><div><p class="eyebrow">Operating principles</p><h2>Maintainable by design.</h2></div><ul class="principle__list"><li>Accessible and responsive interfaces</li><li>Secure named access and least practical privilege</li><li>Open standards and portable source</li><li>Low recurring cost where practical</li><li>Clear testing, documentation, and rollback</li></ul></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
